Robot Return to Origin
📌 Problem

Given a string moves consisting of characters 'U', 'D', 'L', and 'R', determine whether the robot returns to the origin (0,0) after executing all moves.

💡 Approach
Count the number of moves in each direction:
Left (L) vs Right (R)
Up (U) vs Down (D)
The robot returns to origin only if:
L == R and U == D
⚡ Key Idea

Balanced movements cancel each other:

Left cancels Right
Up cancels Down
⏱️ Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

-----------------------------------------------------Solution--------------------------------------------
class Solution {
public:
    bool judgeCircle(string moves) {
        int lf=0, rg=0, up=0, dw=0;

        for(int i=0;i<moves.size();i++){
            if(moves[i]=='L') lf++;
            else if(moves[i]=='R') rg++;
            else if(moves[i]=='U') up++;
            else dw++;
        }

        return (lf==rg && up==dw);
    }
};
